    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0575" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg477"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cambon to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the French Republic</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chicago</hi> of the American Navy, commanded by Rear-Admiral Schley, having
                    met the French steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Bretagne</hi> 60 miles distant
                    from Bahia, having damaged her machinery, towed this vessel in distress as far
                    as Bahia. The Admiral refused all claim for salvage—happy, as he stated, to
                    please a friendly nation.</p>
                <p>The French consul at Bahia at once called upon the consul of the United States at
                    that city, and requested him to transmit his thanks to Admiral Schley.</p>
                <p>My Government, informed of this courteous act of this general officer, was much
                    touched by it, and has directed me to convey to the Government of the United
                    States the expression of its appreciation of it.</p>
                <p>I am happy to be the medium of fulfilling near you this agreeable mission.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jules Cambon</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
